# Local Harness

- Use `uv run lbx-rl-harness reference --problem-dir problems/<task_id>` while iterating on `solution/solve.sh` (train/solve + grade with persistent cache under `.alignerr/reference_cache/output`). Use `--skip-solve` to re-grade cached artifacts, `--no-grade` to train only, and `--clean-cache` to wipe the cache. For `multi_deterministic_rubrics`, reference also refreshes sealed `scorer/evaluation.plan.json` from `TASK` — commit it; never hand-edit.
- Use `uv run lbx-rl-harness run --problem-dir problems/<task_id> --runtime ground-truth` as optional local oracle preflight; this updates local evidence and refreshes the rubric evaluation plan when applicable.
- Use `uv run lbx-rl-harness run --problem-dir problems/<task_id> --runtime agent` for optional local DeepAgents runs (requires API keys in `.env.local`).
- Trusted CI generates authoritative build proof/lock evidence from the immutable PR. Do not commit local generated proof/lock files; commit refreshed `scorer/evaluation.plan.json` and declared reviewed media.
- `lbx-rl-template validate` only **checks** the sealed plan (`check_evaluation_plan`); it does not write it. Trusted CI reseals via an explicit refresh step before validate.
- If an agent can reason but cannot write `/tmp/output/<artifact>`, check that the task Dockerfile includes `WORKDIR /workdir` and `chown -R 1000:1000 /workdir /tmp/output`.
- The harness auto-loads `.env.local`; never read or print `.env.local` contents.
- Use `--runtime solution` only for deterministic reference-solution scorer checks.
- Inspect `.harness-runs/<run>/trajectory.json` and `verifier/reward-details.json` when debugging failures.
- Keep `.env.local` and `.harness-runs/` out of git.
